{"path":"std/fs/fn.copy.html","title":"Function copy","description":"Copies the contents of one file to another. This function will also copy the permission bits of the original file to the destination file.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function copy"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#2833-2835","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"pub fn copy<P: AsRef<Path>, Q: AsRef<Path>>(from: P, to: Q) -> Result<u64>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copies the contents of one file to another. This function will also copy the permission bits of the original file to the destination file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"overwrite"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the contents of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that if "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" both point to the same file, then the file will likely get truncated by this operation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On success, the total number of bytes copied is returned and it is equal to the length of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" file as reported by "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to copy the contents of one file to another and you’re working with "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html","title":"struct std::fs::File","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"File"}]},{"type":"text","value":"s, see the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/fn.copy.html","title":"fn std::io::copy","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"io::copy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"platform-specific-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function currently corresponds to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"open"},{"type":"text","value":" function in Unix with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"O_RDONLY"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"O_WRONLY"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"O_CREAT"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"O_TRUNC"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"O_CLOEXEC"},{"type":"text","value":" is set for returned file descriptors."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Linux (including Android), this function uses copy_file_range(2), sendfile(2), or splice(2) syscalls to move data directly between files if possible."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Windows, this function currently corresponds to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"CopyFileEx"},{"type":"text","value":". Alternate NTFS streams are copied but only the size of the main stream is returned by this function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On MacOS, this function corresponds to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"fclonefileat"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"fcopyfile"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that platform-specific behavior "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/index.html#platform-specific-behavior","title":"mod std::io","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may change in the future"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will return an error in the following situations, but is not limited to just these cases:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" is neither a regular file nor a symlink to a regular file."}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" does not exist."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current process does not have the permission rights to read "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" or write "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parent directory of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" doesn’t exist."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nfn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\n    fs::copy(\"foo.txt\", \"bar.txt\")?;  // Copy foo.txt to bar.txt\n    Ok(())\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Ause+std::fs;%0A%0Afn+main()+-%3E+std::io::Result%3C()%3E+%7B%0A++++fs::copy(%22foo.txt%22,+%22bar.txt%22)?;++//+Copy+foo.txt+to+bar.txt%0A++++Ok(())%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]}]}}
